IMPORT prelude
-- The shapes EVERY can take. Most of the rules below name no group — no
-- `WHO elem t tenants` — so they show the syntax without being runnable:
-- running a quantified rule needs a list to draw the group from, and says so
-- when there is none. See "Where the group comes from" on EVERY.md, and
-- every-run-example.l4 for the same rules with a group and a trace.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor, what IS A STRING
    Pay     HAS payer  IS AN Actor, payee IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER
    Receipt HAS issuer IS AN Actor, to    IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
tenants     MEANS LIST (Tenant OF "Alice"), (Tenant OF "Bob"), (Tenant OF "Carol")

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy begins` MEANS
    PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) what WITHIN 5

-- everyone, then one thing: ONCE ALL HAVE, then HENCE fires once, when the
-- last tenant has signed
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`all tenants sign` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  `the tenancy begins`
        LEST   BREACH

-- each with its own: UPON EACH, then HENCE fires once per tenant who pays
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`each payment gets a receipt` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        MUST   Pay (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY theLandlord) amount
        WITHIN 7
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord
                    MUST   Receipt (EXACTLY theLandlord) (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY amount)
                    WITHIN 5)
        LEST   BREACH BY t

-- a deadline on the whole: each signature within 14, all of them within 30
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`sign, and be done by day 30` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 30
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

-- composed with RAND: the tenants' signatures AND the landlord's delivery
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`sign and deliver` MEANS
    (EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) WITHIN 14 ONCE ALL HAVE HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH)
    RAND
    (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) what WITHIN 14 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH)

-- only some of them: WHO narrows the cast
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the listed tenants sign` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t
        WHO    elem t tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14

-- the bare form: every value of the party type, landlord included
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`everyone signs` MEANS
    EVERY a MUST Sign (EXACTLY a) WITHIN 14
